        "original_id": "2947639b-78bb-5627-8d80-9fdede6cb774",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dean Jones, Laurens van der Post\n- Films: The Million Dollar Duck, A Far Off Place, The Love Bug, Beethoven\n- Television series: Ensign O'Toole\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Organizations: NBC, United States Navy\n- Topics: American comedy films, adventure drama films, literary adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Ensign O'Toole aired on NBC from September 23, 1962, to May 5, 1963.\n- Ensign O'Toole was a military comedy starring 31-year-old Dean Jones as a nonchalant United States Navy ensign in the early 1960s.\n- The Love Bug featured Dean Jones as Jim Douglas in 1968.\n- The Million Dollar Duck was a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Million Dollar Duck was also titled The $1,000,000 Duck and was about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in The Million Dollar Duck in 1971 and received a Golden Globe nomination for the role.\n- Laurens van der Post published A Story Like the Wind in 1972.\n- Laurens van der Post published A Far-Off Place in 1974.\n- Beethoven featured Dean Jones as Dr. Herman Varnick in 1992.\n- A Far Off Place was a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works A Story Like the Wind and A Far-Off Place.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
